<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 22.186 points off FTSE 100 index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 22.186 points off FTSE 100 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stocks went ex-dividend on Monday and the effect was to take 22.186 points off this morning.</p>
<p>							 DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>							 (PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>		   COMPANY			  Net   Gross    Gross</p>
<p> * BAT Industries				 16.00 20.00    3.630</p>
<p> * BTR						 5.60  7.00    1.647</p>
<p> * Cadbury Schweppes			    11.80 14.75    0.863</p>
<p> * GKN						16.90 21.13    0.436</p>
<p> * Glaxo Wellcome				 (c)   22.56    4.681</p>
<p> * HSBC Holdings (75p)			  26.00 32.50    1.655</p>
<p> * HSBC Holdings ($HK)			  26.00 32.50    3.404</p>
<p> * Ladbroke Group				  3.80  4.75    0.326</p>
<p> * RTZ Corporation				18.49 23.11    1.447</p>
<p> * Reuters Holdings				9.00 11.25    1.111</p>
<p> * Royal &amp; Sun Alliance			 12.50 15.63    1.425</p>
<p> * Zeneca Group				   22.50 28.13    1.558</p>
<p>(a) For BAT Industries the total dividend amount is 19.5p and includes 17.5p gross of Foreign Income Dividend (FID).</p>
<p>(b) For BTR the dividend is an FID of 7p gross only.  </p>
<p>(c) For Glaxo Wellcome the total dividend amount is 19p and includes an FID of 4.75p (gross).</p>
<p>(d) For RTZ Corporation the total dividend amount is 21.11p and includes an FID of 13.11p (gross).</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
